    "schema_diff_summary": "movement.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only smart_home_col. A gap is whitespace or U+FEFF. The position test uses one || expression. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not add U+200B. Do not touch is_word_char, smart_home, or move_selection. The existing test smart_home_toggles_indent_and_column_zero stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test smart_home_skips_a_byte_order_mark uses TextBuffer::from_str of U+FEFF, three spaces, and abc. move_selection of SmartHome from Selection::caret of Offset(7) with Extend::No and ctx() has head Offset(4). The same move from that head has head Offset(0). Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
